e-persist-policy\", \"src-guide-storage\", \"src-node-ready-contract\", \"src-storage-envelope\", \"src-ready-advance\"], \"answered\": \"README repeats same-batch concurrent send wording, but independently requires Entries before changed HardState. Ready.Messages remains stricter and raft.send explicitly describes append acknowledgments as persistence-dependent. Therefore a generic immediate-send scenario with a HardState update would not isolate the ambiguity. The selected experiment instead requires an unchanged follower HardState and produces every network response through the implementation.\", \"remaining\": [\"Observe actual producer and consumer effects under the two explicit policies.\", \"Contract applicability of the early-send arm remains unresolved; RawNode exploration does not establish Node permission or a consensus violation.\"], \"understanding\": \"unchanged\", \"rationale\": \"This small conditional experiment determines whether unchanged-HardState batches make the wording conflict consequential at the existing F-persistence-envelope consumer. If observed, retain the precise policy effect and then resolve or bound applicability rather than escalating it automatically to a safety finding.\", \"question_updates\": {}}, \"map_updated\": false, \"map_changes\": {}, \"accepted_versions\": {\"audit_spec\": 1, \"units\": {}, \"artifacts\": {}}, \"candidate_ids\": []}]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
